Bookline exhibits — licence
===========================

This repository accompanies the book *Software Engineering Thinking: Judgment,
Review, and Craft When AI Writes the Code* by Avishek Nag.

It contains three kinds of material with three different statuses. They are
separated deliberately, because a single blanket licence over all of it would
claim rights in work that is not mine to license.


1. WRITTEN MATERIAL — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Covers everything I wrote: the prompts (PROMPT.md), the results and verdicts
(RESULTS.md, VERDICT.md), the diagnostic and seed records (DIAGNOSTIC_RECORD.md,
SEED_RECORD.md), every README, and the selection and arrangement of this
repository as a whole.

    Copyright (c) 2026 Avishek Nag

    This material is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
    International Licence. To view a copy of this licence, visit
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt it, including commercially, provided you give
appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if changes were made.

Suggested attribution:

    Avishek Nag, "Bookline exhibits", companion repository to *Software
    Engineering Thinking* (2026), https://github.com/biddu/bookline,
    licensed CC BY 4.0.


2. CODE I WROTE — MIT Licence
------------------------------

Covers the hand-written source I authored: everything under drafted/, the
diagnostic artefacts I constructed by hand, the core under test, and the test
harness scripts.

Creative Commons recommends against using CC licences for software, because they
say nothing about source distribution or patents and are incompatible with the
common software licences. So the code carries MIT instead.

    MIT License

